Subject: [PATCH 04/12] =?UTF-8?q?fix(masking):=20three=20safety=20holes=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20unmaskable=20PK=20columns,=20dry-run=20side=20effec?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ts,=20PII=20in=20previews?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Sensitive primary-key columns were silently dropped from the UPDATE
   (update_rows never rewrites key columns) while the preview showed them
   as masked. The engine now excludes key columns up front, reports them in
   TableMaskResult.skipped_columns, and the CLI prints an unmissable
   'NOT MASKED — primary-key column' warning.

2. Dry runs persisted (original -> masked) pairs to the seed map. A
   preview now has no side effects: pairs are recorded only when values
   are written. Previews still read existing pairs, and strategies are
   deterministic, so the preview stays an exact prediction of --apply.

3. The mask preview printed original values to the terminal. Originals are
   now redacted shape-only by default (Ada-99 -> ***-**); --show-values
   opts in explicitly.

Also warns when applying with the publicly-known default masking.seed.

